# `vercel deploy` from the repository root, as the release workflow runs it,
# uploads every file these lines don't name. Unlike a Git deployment it never
# reads .gitignore, and its own defaults leave out only .env.local and
# .env.*.local, so without this file any .env or .env.test, which hold
# secrets, would be uploaded. apps/web/.vercelignore has the same lines.
.env*
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.test.example
